<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33605" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pancrătĭum</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-tion</span></b> ), ii,
		n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παγκράτιον</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A complete combat; a gymnastic contest which
				included both wrestling and boxing;</i> cf. <i><span class="en">Quint. 2,
				8, 13</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">et patitur duro volnera pancratio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
					4, 13, 8</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Sen. Ben. 5, 3, 1</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Autolycos pancratio victor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					34, 8, 19, § 79</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. 35, 11, 40, § 139</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Fabr. p. 100</span></i>, n.
			226.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The herb succory</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 20, 8,
				30, § 74</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A plant</i>, <i>called also</i>
			scilla pusilla, <i><span class="en">Plin. 27, 12, 92, §
		118</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
